scope: |
  SSE on the v2 HTTP route, so the server can speak first: `Accept: text/event-stream` holds the
  reply open, frames go out as `data:` events, and `elicit`/`listRoots`/`request` can be answered on
  a second POST while the first is parked. Inbound routing already existed.
  Gate row in v21-standard-mcp-smoke.sh asserting the elicit round trip completes, with the control
  being the same call minus the Accept header. Docs and the BUGS entry updated to match.
next: gate row green, then smoke-ci and push
